WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.583
(upbeat music)

00:00:04.434 --> 00:00:05.775
- [Voiceover] A man is at a restaurant.

00:00:05.775 --> 00:00:07.644
The waiter is like, "Hey, we have a great

00:00:07.644 --> 00:00:08.824
sea bass tonight."

00:00:08.824 --> 00:00:10.817
"Shut up," the man says.

00:00:10.817 --> 00:00:12.811
"I would like a juice glass with water,

00:00:12.811 --> 00:00:15.052
a lemon wedge and a match."

00:00:15.052 --> 00:00:17.003
The waiter is like, "What?

00:00:17.003 --> 00:00:18.295
Okay, you weirdo."

00:00:18.295 --> 00:00:20.206
The man pours the water onto the plate.

00:00:20.206 --> 00:00:22.199
He's like, "If you can get this water

00:00:22.199 --> 00:00:24.234
into this glass without touching or moving

00:00:24.234 --> 00:00:28.910
this here plate, I will
give you a 100 dollar tip,

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:31.433
one hundo dollar ruskies."

00:00:31.433 --> 00:00:35.330
That night the waiter walked
home 100 dollars richer.

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:36.747
How did he do it?

00:00:37.732 --> 00:00:38.565
- Em.

00:00:39.504 --> 00:00:42.064
- You have to be some kind of sorcerer,

00:00:42.064 --> 00:00:44.695
some kind of magician or god.

00:00:44.695 --> 00:00:47.160
- (sighs)

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:51.327
- If my junior high science
class taught me anything,

00:00:52.367 --> 00:00:54.805
I think I might remember how
to do something like this.

00:00:54.805 --> 00:00:57.107
- I think like the lemon is for the water

00:00:57.107 --> 00:00:59.503
after he drinks, he's gonna drink it.

00:00:59.503 --> 00:01:01.777
The water and he wants
lemon for the water.

00:01:01.777 --> 00:01:03.567
- I like 100 percent have to light

00:01:03.567 --> 00:01:07.028
this lemon wedge on fire I think.

00:01:07.028 --> 00:01:08.309
- Fuck you wedge.

00:01:08.309 --> 00:01:09.242
- That's what I feel right?

00:01:09.242 --> 00:01:12.798
Yeah, it kind of feel,
I just can't figure out.

00:01:12.798 --> 00:01:16.524
- I just need to keep the
air inside, inside here

00:01:16.524 --> 00:01:20.346
so I'm guessing I just
need to, interesting.

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:22.429
- There's gotta be a way.

00:01:24.704 --> 00:01:26.168
- Are you supposed to light the match?

00:01:26.168 --> 00:01:28.164
Does the fire help?

00:01:28.164 --> 00:01:30.035
- Feel like it's just the surface tension

00:01:30.035 --> 00:01:33.785
on the, on the water,
not on the heat inside.

00:01:35.651 --> 00:01:37.116
- Did I get it right?

00:01:37.116 --> 00:01:37.949
- Kind of.

00:01:37.949 --> 00:01:40.446
- This is bologna (chuckling).

00:01:40.446 --> 00:01:42.597
- [Voiceover] So, what's the right answer?

00:01:42.597 --> 00:01:44.347
Well, first the waiter put the lemon

00:01:44.347 --> 00:01:45.812
in the center of the plate,

00:01:45.812 --> 00:01:48.705
then he lit the match and
stuck it in the lemon.

00:01:48.705 --> 00:01:50.530
Then he placed the glass upside

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:51.833
over the lemon.

00:01:51.833 --> 00:01:54.602
As the match's flame used
up the oxygen in the glass,

00:01:54.602 --> 00:01:56.998
it created a vacuum
which sucked in the water

00:01:56.998 --> 00:01:58.668
where the glass met the plate.

00:01:58.668 --> 00:02:01.271
So the waiter was able to
get the water into the glass

00:02:01.271 --> 00:02:03.144
without moving the plate.

00:02:03.144 --> 00:02:04.513
